<title>USA: Republicans agreed to $33 bln US airline tax revs.</title>
<headline>Republicans agreed to $33 bln US airline tax revs.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>House and Senate Republicans in a unified tax proposal to be discussed with White House officials agreed to raise revenues by $33 billion over five years through airline taxes, a key Republican said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We've agreed to a $33 billion revenue stream from what we call the ticket tax,&quot; House Ways and Means Committee Chairman Bill Archer, a Texas Republican, said. &quot;It is a very, very comprehensive package that stands together.&quot;</p>
<p>He would not give details on what the airline tax package included. The separate House and Senate tax bills had raised about $34 billion in revenues over five years from airline taxes and fees.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
